ba58b7a6dffb78256fc95e078d6739" commit_message="Turn authpolicy on for everything except arm  Some dependencies don't compile on arm (yet). The original plan was to turn authpolicy on for some boards only. However, we decided to turn it on for all x86-based boards, so we hit problems rather sooner than later.  BUG=chromium:667696 TEST=Used emerge to display dependencies, made sure logic for toggling works.  Change-Id: I4db46e503df117f029aa2ebc6dc5f4c8e321de19 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/415324 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="415324" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/24/415324/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0e90259e2a0b29fa9cb9178a13327dcc40cb1b80" commit="e0db9718bcc4d13460c82604dffc2922c5996b22" commit_message="Add missing dependencies for authpolicy  Was missing protobuf, system_api, dbus and test deps. Also needs to depend on the protofiles-0.0.2 because that provides some .py script and a .json file.  BUG=None TEST=Emerges  Change-Id: I0e90259e2a0b29fa9cb9178a13327dcc40cb1b80 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414871 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="414871" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/71/414871/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2fc0b8304468aab2757593a56f50e1f0a41fe3b1" commit="3e296c24f32fb25b392676428c33be7dfae93869" commit_message="installer: Ensure that the squashfs doesn't written to during install  MakeFileSystemRw only works on filesystems which can be made writable, but doesn't check ensure that the filesystem is writable at all. This change checks that if the filesystem has the squashfs id at the beginning, and if so, does not modify it at all.  Also, it removes the unused &quot;rw&quot; argument from &quot;MakeFileSystemRw&quot; Given its name, it should always make the filesystem rw, and is currently always used that way.  BUG=chromium:666530  TEST=I did good things.  Change-Id: I2fc0b8304468aab2757593a56f50e1f0a41fe3b1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/412271 Commit-Ready: Matthew Mirman &lt;mirman@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Matthew Mirman &lt;mirman@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="412271" owner_email="mirman@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/71/412271/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If30e19a6f83462cce2f5b593da9d2f8f8a5796fd" commit="6ac4c15876355b795b0994f1902083541963205d" commit_message="Gale: Add board ID and memory type support  Upcoming hardware change for Gale will have two different memory chips (Samsung and Nanya) so mosys had to be updated to check board ID and return proper memory type.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:60053 TEST=Use variable-board type firmware, try board ID 8,10 and other TEST=&quot;memory spd print id&quot;, check Nanya for ID 8,10, Samsung for other BRANCH=none  Change-Id: If30e19a6f83462cce2f5b593da9d2f8f8a5796fd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/414312 Commit-Ready: Yuji Sasaki &lt;sasakiy@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yuji Sasaki &lt;sasakiy@google.